// Title: an arm that takes a part out of an `Any` scrutinee and decides it a
// reference in its body passes the check; any reference passes the run-time
// test, so an i64 is written into a string variable.
// Command: graphix --no-cache x-typecheck-patterns-any-arm-decides-ref.gx
//   (and `--check`, which exits 0)
// Expected: the check refuses the arm, as it refuses the written test
//   `(&mut i64, i64) as (r, n)` over Any ("can't tell what the reference in
//   .. refers to where the scrutinee may hold Any") and an arm that decides
//   the part a function type ("can't match on a type holding a function").
// Observed: --check exits 0. The run prints "s = str, out = 4", then the
//   runtime thread panics:
//     kernel param `s`: runtime I64(2) does not match the compiled String slot
//     Error: runtime did not respond
//   Under --no-fusion the string variable `s` silently holds 2.
// The read-only form is unsound the same way:
//   |x: Any| select x { (r, n) => { let q: &i64 = r; *q + n }, _ => 0 }
// reads a `&string` as an i64 ("arith error .. Unexpected `s`").
let f = |x: Any| select x { (r, n) => { *r <- n + 1; 0 }, _ => 0 };
let s = "str";
let v: Any = (&mut s, 1);
let k = |a: string, b: string| str::len(a) + str::len(b);
f(v);
let out = k(s, "x");
println("s = [s], out = [out]");
sys::exit(sys::time::after_idle(duration:200.ms, 0));
out
